"""zorro-sweep: clean up a big notes vault one note at a time.

  Keep or delete   a note fills the screen; swipe it left to keep, right to delete
  Sort             the kept notes, one by one; drag each onto the notebook it belongs in
                   (another vault, or a folder in this one); the best match by meaning lights up

Swipe = drag with the mouse or a finger on the touch screen, or two fingers on the touchpad.
Keys: ← keep · → delete · Space skip · Ctrl+Z undo · O open in Obsidian · 1-9 notebook (Sort)
      Enter: best notebook (Sort)

Delete moves the note (and pictures only it uses) to the vault's .trash folder, Obsidian's own
trash: gone from the vault and from your phone, still on this laptop if you need it back.
Moving to another vault takes the note's pictures along.

  zorro-sweep [--vault PATH]     default: the vault called Notes (else the biggest one)

Progress: ~/.local/state/zorro-sweep/<vault>.json (which notes you kept)
"""
